  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>World Bank, World Development Indicators, data.worldbank.org: manufacturing value added (share of GDP, constant 2015 US$ level, annual growth) and industry share from national accounts via UNIDO/OECD; the technology decomposition from UNIDO; manufactures' share of merchandise exports from UN Comtrade. Vintage <b id="prov-vintage" set:html={N["prov-vintage"]} /> (the WDI database last-updated stamp, not the fetch date). Four bundles are baked: the headline accounts (1960–2025), the UNIDO composition (1963–2023), the technology share (1990–2022) and the export share (1962–2024).</p>
        <p><b>Coverage note.</b> This is the atlas's first World Bank guide; the twelve others are Indian official statistics. Manufacturing here is ISIC Section C from the national accounts: a different ruler from the Annual Survey of Industries' registered factories (Guide 08), and the two are never compared level-for-level.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions &amp; uncertainty</h6>
        <p>The WDI revises history freely as member countries rebase their national accounts; no figure here is final, including the oldest. This guide quotes the vintage with the value for exactly that reason. The four bundles end in different years, 2025, 2024, 2023, 2022, because their source agencies report on different lags; the gaps are shown, never filled. Where a later year is unmeasured, this guide says "we do not know" rather than inventing a number.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Output, version 1.0, covers manufacturing value added (share, level, growth), the UNIDO technology composition, manufactures' share of exports and the medium- &amp; high-tech share. Next scheduled revision: on the next WDI database update.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
